elds ["q-105178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "49251196-c06b-5718-82e6-5ed9450301af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7163"] :question/problem "Let $U = \\{ a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\}$ be the universal set and let $B = \\{ b, d, f \\}.$ What is $\\overline{B}?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/25f40492b0466495519d6ff94859d0cef4c206e291d31eba2a980732b497af31.png)" :question/worked-solution "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overline B,$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $B.$ To represent $\\overline B,$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $B,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/daad235ef63e127e99bf3eec7b7bbe75fe6adb969f5b54ebb5a3fb010773b680.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a,$ $c,$ $e,$ and $g.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $B.$ Therefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{B} = \\{ a,c,e,g \\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
